WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.251 --> 00:00:02.668
(slow music)

00:00:03.981 --> 00:00:06.598
- Eagle feathers give us
that strength and courage

00:00:06.598 --> 00:00:07.431
to go on.

00:00:10.291 --> 00:00:13.962
They've been in our
ceremonies for centuries.

00:00:13.962 --> 00:00:17.141
And to be able to have these feathers

00:00:17.141 --> 00:00:20.240
in our time of prayer,
in our time of need,

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.428
is really important to us.

00:00:22.428 --> 00:00:25.428
(slow upbeat music)

00:00:26.677 --> 00:00:29.674
- We're at the National Eagle Repository.

00:00:29.674 --> 00:00:32.532
Last year we received
right at 2,700 eagles

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:35.581
that were found dead or died
for one reason or another

00:00:35.581 --> 00:00:38.304
and we provide loose feathers from eagles

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:40.409
to Native Americans for their religious

00:00:40.409 --> 00:00:42.242
and cultural purposes.

00:00:43.199 --> 00:00:44.828
They are protected by various laws

00:00:44.828 --> 00:00:47.170
such as the Bald and
Golden Eagle Protection Act

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:50.367
so people can't just go picking them up.

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:51.839
But this way, it allows Native Americans

00:00:51.839 --> 00:00:55.339
a lawful way to obtain and possess eagles.

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:00.439
The birds that we get have
died from various causes.

00:01:00.439 --> 00:01:02.319
They often collide with something

00:01:02.319 --> 00:01:03.770
that causes them to break a wing

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:06.621
and, of course, results in death,

00:01:06.621 --> 00:01:08.508
but usually those
injuries are pretty minor

00:01:08.508 --> 00:01:10.170
to the feathers, so we could still use

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.269
most of the feathers.

00:01:12.269 --> 00:01:14.478
So we're checking what
needs to be replaced there

00:01:14.478 --> 00:01:16.919
or what feathers need to be added in,

00:01:16.919 --> 00:01:18.269
in an effort to try to
give them the equivalent

00:01:18.269 --> 00:01:19.769
of one whole bird.

00:01:21.301 --> 00:01:23.247
- The role of the
National Eagle Repository,

00:01:23.247 --> 00:01:24.690
it's very important.

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:28.719
It helps us to keep going with our lives

00:01:28.719 --> 00:01:30.052
that we know it.

00:01:31.279 --> 00:01:33.558
- It's good to know that
you're a part of something

00:01:33.558 --> 00:01:36.132
that means so much to a group of people

00:01:36.132 --> 00:01:38.150
and that you're playing a role

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:41.483
in protecting a very treasured resource.

